---
Title: Beef Tenderloin with Red Wine Sauce
Servings: 4-6 servings
Tags: Prospects, American, Beef, Roast, Tenderloin, Red Wine
Link: https://www.onceuponachef.com/recipes/roast-beef-tenderloin-wine-sauce.html
---

Preheat the oven to 400°F with an oven rack set in the middle position.

Let @Beef Tenderloin Roast{1 (2.5 lb)} stand at room temperature for ~{1 hour} before roasting.

Melt @Unsalted Butter{5 tbsp} in a #medium saucepan{}. Add finely chopped @Shallots{3/4 cup} and cook over medium-low heat until soft and translucent, ~{7-8 minutes}.

Add @Red Wine{1 1/4 cups}, @Beef Broth{3 cups}, @Fresh Thyme Sprigs{6}, @Salt{1/4 tsp}, @Black Pepper{1/8 tsp}, and @Sugar{1 tsp}. Bring to a boil, then cook over medium heat for ~{30 minutes}, or until the liquid is reduced by half.

In a #small bowl{}, combine remaining @Unsalted Butter{3 tbsp} (softened) and @Flour{2 tbsp}. Mix together with a #spoon into a smooth paste (beurre manié).

Reduce heat to low and remove the thyme sprigs from the reduced wine sauce. Whisk the flour-butter paste into the simmering liquid a teaspoonful at a time, and simmer for ~{2-3 minutes} until the sauce is thickened. Set aside.

Season the beef tenderloin all over with @Salt{1 1/2 tsp} (1/2 tsp per lb) and @Black Pepper{3/4 tsp} (1/4 tsp per lb).

Heat @Vegetable Oil{2 tbsp} in an #oven-proof skillet{} over medium-high heat until almost smoking. Cook the beef, turning with #tongs, until well browned on all but one side, ~{10 minutes} total.

Turn the tenderloin so that the un-seared side is down, and transfer the skillet directly to the preheated oven.

Roast until a thermometer inserted into the center of the meat registers 120°F-125°F for medium-rare, ~{15 minutes}.

Transfer the beef to a #carving board{} and let it rest, covered loosely with aluminum foil, for ~{10-15 minutes}.

Carefully discard the excess fat from the skillet. Place the skillet on the stovetop over medium heat, add @Beef Broth{1/4 cup}, and bring to a boil while scraping up the browned bits from the bottom of the pan with a #wooden spoon{}.

Pour the deglazed pan juices into the wine sauce and bring to a simmer.

Carve the beef tenderloin into 1/3-inch-thick slices and serve with the warm red wine sauce.